# The OpenBot images the server, computer and supervisor run from.
#
# Every way of running OpenBot from this checkout pulls them by this one tag:
#
#   ghcr.io/copilotkit/openbot, the one image the server and every Bot's computer run from, each
#   started with its own command, and ghcr.io/copilotkit/openbot-supervisor.
#
# The tag is `main` on the main branch: the images built from main, which move with every build.
# A release pins its own version here (`v1.0.3` in the v1.0.3 tag), which never moves, so a
# checkout of a release runs that release's images. The release PR writes the version, and main
# gets `main` back after a stable release.
#
# Read by scripts/start.sh, which pulls the images at this tag on every start, CI, the release and
# internal-build workflows and Desktop's local build (desktop/scripts/local-build.sh), each of which
# hands it to Compose as OPENBOT_BACKEND_TAG. An
# OPENBOT_BACKEND_TAG in the environment or in .env wins over this line, to run another build.
# Running Compose by hand, pass this file first and .env after it, so .env still wins:
#
#   docker compose --env-file backend-images.env --env-file .env up -d
OPENBOT_BACKEND_TAG=main
